' ===== ANNOTATIONS =====
note right of patients
  **PostgreSQL RLS Policies**
  - staff_own_department: staff can only
    view patients they've treated or
    are assigned to their department
  - patient_self_access: patients can
    view their own records via portal
  - audit_logs capture every access
end note

note right of pharmacy_batches
  **Batch & Expiry Tracking**
  - FIFO consumption enforced at dispense
  - EXPIRED status auto-set via cron
  - QUARANTINE for damaged/recalled stock
  - Critical in Zim: supply chain disruptions
    cause variable expiry dates per batch
end note

note right of billing_invoices
  **Multi-Currency Billing (USD/ZiG)**
  - invoice in service currency
  - base_currency_total for reporting
  - Medical aid claims tracked separately
  - Supports cash, Ecocash, Zipit, bank
  - exchange_rate locked at invoice time
end note

note right of lab_results
  **Critical Result Alerting**
  - is_critical flag triggers immediate
    notification to attending doctor
  - critical_notified_at tracks response
  - Interpretation guides treatment urgency
end note

note bottom of clinical_document_chunks
  **pgvector: Clinical RAG Pipeline**
  --
  1. PDF guidelines ingested into sources
  2. Chunked with overlap (512 tokens, 50 overlap)
  3. Each chunk embedded via local model
     (all-MiniLM-L6-v2, CPU, no API needed)
  4. HNSW index for sub-10ms similarity search
  5. Doctor query -> embed -> top_k chunks -> LLM context
  --
  **SQL:**
  SELECT chunk_text, 1 - (chunk_text_embedding <=> query_vec)
  FROM clinical_document_chunks
  WHERE source_id = ANY(guideline_ids)
  ORDER BY chunk_text_embedding <=> query_vec
  LIMIT 5;
end note

note bottom of patient_clinical_embeddings
  **pgvector: Patient Similarity Search**
